      "reason": "S2.1.3.p1 defines four groups of n=3 male rats (untrained LRT/HRT, trained LRTT/HRTT; separate cohorts, not pre/post on the same animals). S3.2.p3 states the exercise-response analysis compares each trained group to its untrained counterpart; this is the within-line training effect, the estimand closest to 'how exercise affects gene expression'. Fig 2C/S3.2.p1 is the headline HRTT vs LRTT contrast (255 DEGs, FC>1.5, FDR<0.05). Exact paper counts for the training contrasts are not stated in the text, so they are taken from the authors' deposited Cuffdiff lists, all of whose rows pass q<0.05 and |log2FC|>log2(1.5) (HRTT/LRTT list reproduces the text's 255 = 68 up / 187 down exactly).",
